        "## Example 2\n",
        "\n",
        "Let's scrape data on the super bowl results and winners. To this end, we will use the website: <https://www.foxsports.com/nfl-super-bowl-winners-and-results>\n",
        "\n",
        "![](images/superbowl.png){fig-align=\"center\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "## \n",
        "\n",
        "</br></br>\n",
        "\n",
        "Using **requests**, we first download the HTML code of the webpage.\n",
        "\n",
        "Then, we use **BeautifulSoup** to parse the HTML document."
      ],
      "id": "92580448"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| echo: true\n",
        "#| output: true\n",
        "\n",
        "url = \"https://www.foxsports.com/nfl-super-bowl-winners-and-results\"\n",
        "\n",
        "response = requests.get(url)\n",
        "\n",
        "superbowl_website = BeautifulSoup(response.text, \"html.parser\")"
      ],
      "id": "6c250aff",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## The output"
      ],
      "id": "acd6f7d6"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| echo: true\n",
        "#| output: true\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "superbowl_website"
      ],
      "id": "46f25bc7",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Now, let's inspect the elements using SelectorGadget\n",
        "\n",
        "</br></br>\n",
        "\n",
        "![](images/superbowl_paragraph.png){fig-align=\"center\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "## \n",
        "\n",
        "We scrape elements of a website stored in `superbowl_website` using the `select()` function.\n",
        "\n",
        "For example, we can retrieve all paragraph elements (`<p>content<\\p>`). To this end, we set the CSS selector to \"p\"."
      ],
      "id": "f3b15161"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| echo: true\n",
        "\n",
        "sb_web_p = superbowl_website.select(\"p\")\n",
        "\n",
        "sb_web_p"
      ],
      "id": "f08c834a",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## \n",
        "\n",
        "</br>\n",
        "\n",
        "However, the scraped elements are in HTML code.\n",
        "\n",
        "To turn them into actual text for Python, we use the `get_text()` function."
      ],
      "id": "70a64620"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| echo: true\n",
        "\n",
        "# Start a list to store paragraphs\n",
        "superbowl_web_paragraph = []\n",
        "\n",
        "# Clean and store each paragraph\n",
        "for paragraph in sb_web_p:\n",
        "  cleaned_paragraph = paragraph.get_text(strip=True)\n",
        "  superbowl_web_paragraph.append(cleaned_paragraph)\n",
        "\n",
        "superbowl_web_paragraph"
      ],
      "id": "47f83c40",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# \n",
        "\n",
